  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe lathe axis reader reads a short turned bar about its true axis instead of refusing it as \"every axis fits\".\n\n- Cause: the r10×40 bar alone sits just under the isotropy threshold. One modelled radial hole tips it over, and even with the check skipped it drags the plain least-squares line 0.39 mm off the axis, so it's refused anyway.\n- New `multiaxis/axis_poles.rs`: facing flats as candidate axes. Facets sharing one normal (a normal and its opposite count as one axis) that carry ≥ 5% of the area become candidates, up to 3. They're always offered beside the two eigenvector candidates, which are unreliable near isotropy, and they're the only candidates when the moment is isotropic. Eigen candidates win ties. The existing concurrency and coarseness tests still decide which passes.\n- Hole drag: if the plain line about a flat-end candidate fails, it's refit on the half of the normal lines that miss it least, iterated until that half stops changing. It must then pass the full test over every facet.\n- A sphere has no flat and a cube's faces fail coarseness, so both are still refused by name.\n- `axis::try_axis` and `axis_robust::dist` are now visible to sibling modules. `axis.rs` is 399 lines.\n\n## Pins\n\n- `drilling_cross_spindle::a_short_punched_bar_reads_as_turned_about_its_axis` (r10×40 with one hole, axis within 1e-6): **fails on main**\n- `axis_poles::tests::an_l_d_1_5_bar_fits_its_true_axis_lying_down`: **fails on main**\n- `an_l_d_2_bar_fits_its_true_axis`, `a_cube_is_still_refused_by_name`, `a_sphere_is_still_refused_by_name`\n\n## Readings\n\n- motion: lib 134, multiaxis*, rotary* green\n- app: drill_reach, drilling_cross* (all), lathe_cross_drill, lathe_spindle_*, turning and turning_* green\n- clippy on motion and app is clean\n- `punched_bar` stays at L/D 5; a shorter bar with three holes plus mirrors still fails\n\nChangelog: The lathe axis reader reads a short turned bar (L/D about 0.5-2) about its true axis from its facing flats instead of refusing it as \"every axis fits\"; spheres and cubes are still refused\n\nFixes #152\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
